  "review": {
    "generation": "model is rendered from the compiled core by crates/secret-scan-core/src/evidence/aggregate/artifact_drift.rs; its failing assertion prints the rendering. sources are SHA-256 hashes of the listed files and spec sections, including the maintainer-local evaluation path (evidence/shadow.rs and its spec section), so a change to its record format is a new revision. calibration, corpora and tuningManifest are copied from the benchmark run's identities and hashes, never from its fitted detail.",
    "method": "Reviewed in the pull request that changes this file. The reviewer confirms that a changed model carries a new model identity (and a changed featureSchema a new feature schema identity), that every change raises artifact.revision, and that no probability, score, weight or threshold reaches a public surface.",
    "reviewedIn": "https://github.com/redact-secret/redact-secret/issues/771",
    "check": "npm run scoring-artifact:check (offline, part of npm run ci); the cargo test the_compiled_scorer_matches_the_reviewed_scoring_artifact; and the pull-request CI job that runs the same check against the base branch's artifact."
